  "goodToKnow": "Das Niemandsland is no man's land, the strip between front lines or borders, as in the trenches of the First World War. The Berlin Wall's guarded strip was called der Todesstreifen (death strip). Colloquially, im Niemandsland means in the middle of nowhere, and figuratively a grey area: rechtliches Niemandsland. It has no plural."
